cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use NeuroFly, please cite the software as below. If you use the
  connectome data, also cite the MaleCNS paper (the data are CC BY 4.0 and
  require attribution); see the references and NOTICE.
type: software
title: "Project NeuroFly"
abstract: >-
  NeuroFly runs a spiking leaky-integrate-and-fire model of the MaleCNS v1.0
  Drosophila connectome and couples it to an articulated FlyGym/MuJoCo body,
  with a browser dashboard and headless experiment runners. It is research
  software: the connectome has not yet been shown to compute behaviour on its
  own, and the README states what the committed receipts do and do not show.
authors:
  - name: "Project NeuroFly contributors"
version: 0.4.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/average-user-887/flybrain"
url: "https://github.com/average-user-887/flybrain"
keywords:
  - Drosophila
  - connectome
  - MaleCNS
  - spiking neural network
  - neuromechanical simulation
  - FlyGym
